---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Tours and Prices">
<h1>Tours and Prices</h1>
<p>Click on a tour to view more details:</p>

<ul class="tour-list">
<li class="tour-item">
<button class="tour-toggle">
Illapani Waterfall and Chocolate Farm - Day Tour
<span class="arrow">▼</span>
</button>
<div class="tour-details">
<p>Itinerary:</p>
<p>8:00 am depart from Quillabamba - our shuttle will pick you up from your hotel</p>
<p>Hike for approximately 40 minutes to reach the Illapani waterfall</p>
<p>After some photos and a swim, we will drive to the Chahuares Chocolate farm for a tour of the growing and manufacturing process, and a taste of fresh chocolate</p>
<p>Enjoy a traditional Peruvian lunch and relax at the farm</p>
<p>We will head back to Quillabamba in the afternoon, around 4:00 pm </p>
<p>  </p>
<p><strong>Price:</strong> $45 USD</p>
</div>
</li>

<li class="tour-item">
<button class="tour-toggle">
Duende Waterfall and Coffee Farm - Day Tour
<span class="arrow">▼</span>
</button>
<div class="tour-details">
<p>Itinerary:</p>
<p>Depart from Quillabamba at 9:00 am - we will pick you up from your hotel</p>
<p>After a scenic 45 minute drive, we will reach the D'Morveli coffee farm</p>
<p>We will hike for about 30 minutes through cofee fields to reach the Duende Waterfall, where you can go for a swim and take pictures</p>
<p>Then we will return to the farm for a tour and lesson on how coffee is grown and prepared, including samples of 4 varieties of coffee. </p>
<p>After the coffee tour, enjoy a traditional Peruvian lunch at the farm</p>
<p>We will return to Quillabmamba in the afternoon, and drop you off at your accommodation</p>
<p></p>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Price:</strong> $45 USD</p>
</div>
</li>

<li class="tour-item">
<button class="tour-toggle">
Canopy Zipline and Thermal Baths - Day Tour
<span class="arrow">▼</span>
</button>
<div class="tour-details">
<p>Adrenaline and relaxation all in one day</p>
<p>8:30 am depart from Quillabamba - our shuttle will pick you up from your hotel</p>
<p>We'll drive for an hour and fifteen minutes through the scenic Andes mountains to reach Santa Theresa, then from there it is 15 more minutes to the zipline</p>
<p>Gear up with a harness and helmet,then itś time to zipline! You will do a full circuit that includes a 500m, 800m, and 1km zipline, and a bride walk over the treetops</p>
<p>Enjoy a traditional Peruvian lunch while looking out at the forest canopy</p>
<p>After lunch, we will head to the thermal baths of Cocalmayo, where you can swim and relax in multiple pools of different temperatures</p>
<p>Our shuttle will take you back to Quillabamba in the afternoon</p>
<p><strong>Price:</strong> $55 USD</p>
</div>
</li>

<li class="tour-item">
<button class="tour-toggle">
Yanay Mandor Waterfall and White Water Rafting - Day Tour
<span class="arrow">▼</span>
</button>
<div class="tour-details">
<p>Itinerary</p>
<p>8:30 am depart from Quillabamba - our shuttle will pick you up from your hotel</p>
<p>We'll drive for 50 minutes through the scenic Andes mountains to reach the start of the trail</p>
<p>Hike for approximately 35 minutes to reach the Yanay Mandor waterfall, where you can swim and take pictures</p>
<p>Hike back to the Yanay farm to try some of the local coffee and have a traditional Peruvian lunch</p>
<p>After lunch, we will drive to Vilcanota and begin our rafting journey</p>
<p>Experience the thrill of whitewater rafting over 6km, about 2 hours</p>
<p>Our shuttle will take you back to your hotel in Quillabamba in the afternoon</p>
<p><strong>Price:</strong> $60 USD</p>
</div>
</li>

<li class="tour-item">
<button class="tour-toggle">
Amazonian Waterfall Valley Camping - 2 Day Tour
<span class="arrow">▼</span>
</button>
<div class="tour-details">
<p>Itinerary</p>
<p>Day 1</p>
<p>2:30 am depart from Quillabamba - our shuttle will pick you up from your hotel</p>
<p>We'll drive for 5 hours through to reach the river port at Ivochote </p>
<p>Enjoy a traditional Peruvian breakfast in Ivochote before boarding the boat</p>
<p>Admire the increadible nature of the Amazon as we cruise the Urubamba and Yoyato rivers, through the Megantoni Nature Reserve</p>
<p>Upon arrival at our campsite, we will setup tents and settle in </p>
<p>Savor the local delicacy of fried Paco fish for lunch (vegetarian meals can be made upon request)</p>
<p>After lunch we will take a tour of the Yoyato river and bathe in the turquoise water</p>
<p>In the evening we will have dinner and then prepare a campfire where you will learn about the legends of the Pongo de Mainique, and the local communities of the Urubamba river</p>
<p>Spend a magical night under the stars in the Amazon</p>
<p> </p>
<p>Day 2</p>
<p>In the morning we will take a boatride through the magnificent Pongo de Mainique, a canyon lined with waterfalls. </p>
<p>Get a chance to see the Osheto, a mountain in the shape of a monkey that protects the entrance of these ancestral lands</p>
<p>Meet our local guide Pando, and enjoy a traditional breakfast in his home while learning about the local customs</p>
<p>Return once again through the Pongo de Mainique, this time with a deeper understanding of the cultural context and the magic of the region</p>
<p>we will return to Ivochote by boat, and have lunch before returning to Quillabamba by shuttle</p>
<p> </p>
<p><strong>Price:</strong> $120 USD</p>
</div>
</li>
</ul>
<script type="text/javascript">
document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
const toggles = document.querySelectorAll('.tour-toggle');

toggles.forEach((toggle) => {
toggle.addEventListener('click', () => {
const details = toggle.nextElementSibling;
const arrow = toggle.querySelector('.arrow');

// Toggle visibility
details.classList.toggle('open');

// Toggle arrow direction
arrow.textContent = details.classList.contains('open') ? '▲' : '▼';
});
});
});
</script>

<style>
.tour-list {
list-style: none;
padding: 0;
margin: 0;
}

.tour-item {
margin-bottom: 1rem;
border: 1px solid #ccc;
border-radius: 6px;
overflow: hidden;
}

.tour-toggle {
width: 100%;
background: none;
border: none;
padding: 1rem;
text-align: left;
font-size: 1.2rem;
font-weight: bold;
cursor: pointer;
background-color: #f5f5f5;
display: flex;
justify-content: space-between;
align-items: center;
}

.tour-toggle:hover {
background-color: #e5e5e5;
}

.tour-details {
display: none;
padding: 1rem;
background-color: #fff;
}

.tour-details.open {
display: block;
}

.arrow {
font-size: 1rem;
transition: transform 0.3s ease;
}
</style>
</Layout>
